so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(0.55)^{x-1}(0.45), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X\\le 7) & =P(X\\in {4,5,6,7}) \\\\  & =P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =f(4)+f(5)+f(6)+f(7) \\\\  & =(0.55)^{3}(0.45)+(0.55)^{4}(0.45)+(0.55)^{5}(0.45)+(0.55)^{6}(0.45) \\\\  & ≈0.1512.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130226/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335456/field-1/2aae1fb960e1e0244e9e162e527963180777266116a820b7fa5a5d2301f87690" :answer/id #uuid "1ed1307a-0a2c-524d-bc67-9054acc91a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335456/field-1/3130eae0612a9707ae439a5de71c2dcd1a9fc8f90eb61498d0538ba40b4cf834" :answer/id #uuid "ad57b5a1-16a0-5263-9788-9430be98b3c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335456/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b49cc017-9cb2-51a8-ac39-27a17d7b6fc9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335456/field-1/2aae1fb960e1e0244e9e162e527963180777266116a820b7fa5a5d2301f87690" :answer-field/choices ["q-335456/field-1/2aae1fb960e1e0244e9e162e527963180777266116a820b7fa5a5d2301f87690" "q-335456/field-1/3130eae0612a9707ae439a5de71c2dcd1a9fc8f90eb61498d0538ba40b4cf834"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335456" :question/id #uuid "5e8aecb5-e2b4-59a1-aead-447f10577d01" :question/math-academy-id "q-335456" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(1<X<4).$\n\n$P(1<X<4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{4}), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<4) & =P(X\\in {2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{4})+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335456/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130206/selection/8a961fbe78481ed3f2710229c339dd8eea633296f7af1a507775c504092eadd6" :answer/id #uuid "55593944-6374-5268-95ba-f3aea3233d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130206/selection/e3f24454ad345b52c3bd83e065c3234b9827468595eecee3484c0f10261bb218" :answer/id #uuid "f34e52b0-b56e-5848-ab5d-9cd4fb5c5677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130206/selection/c936f526c80adfacd711df9decbe5d1ec9dbea02ce1693ae73b390e483368953" :answer/id #uuid "f3254a75-8f0e-56ea-be2e-c1e1e7f811c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130206/selection/2b7087374d6bbed6228839aee9b5b9546a5e0ef9126b8a20143808d62c399fb1" :answer/id #uuid "712d5c9c-935d-535e-a8be-48c97edaeafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130206/selection/b1a8f37ea2e2ef33dc25928a55f0248f9f6a9f9214af0a976285bf36bdaf35e0" :answer/id #uuid "48779271-0c75-58ee-a31e-b18a6d310054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/