/id #uuid "688411cb-4042-5ded-9f38-8c3face1b1ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-97178" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ compute $P(X\\ge 4)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.6)}^{x-1}(0.4), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 4.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.6)}^{0}(0.4)+{(0.6)}^{1}(0.4)+{(0.6)}^{2}(0.4) \\\\  & =0.784.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4) \\\\  & =1-0.784 \\\\  & =0.216.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130236/selection/8a7ba0513ee4ab7b7ffcf56f49237b44de61fead1a7e775abb18dc3c9bb4fa6a" :answer/id #uuid "070bda51-6387-5fc7-a72d-5d8a2928e27f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9959" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130236/selection/ef26c382f4901972ca4d727274ef6f33777a9a8fd751e198428a6c329978bd59" :answer/id #uuid "240d4020-f490-5684-89a9-b9af56b87459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0041" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130236/selection/d6088d4d59a6add9355c03e4d5a5fdf24d855225b944a9f6f561e49a03874192" :answer/id #uuid "e81288eb-4a4