nitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 6.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =1-P(X<6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<6) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4)+f(5) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{0}(\\frac{2}{3})+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}(\\frac{2}{3})+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3})+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}(\\frac{2}{3})+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & ≈0.9959.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =1-P(X<6) \\\\  & ≈1-0.9959 \\\\  & =0.0041.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130236/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130236"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection/308676ee768935887597226eda63df3da76ab9c572f196f1924a76655ad73d6d" :answer/id #uuid "c808a995-a670-53bc-afb4-c51911634304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1681" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection/f75878873391a8e8308fe21dad7c6dc11f9b4bac31093cc78c4db8e407a5de20" :answer/id #uuid "5dbab6d8-57be-5c67-ac26-2415065f10d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4176" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection/d4cfd0801c2aff2cc8d8f0cdb705bc454b1338fe18b3a150e670f4b9fc2a70a3" :answer/id #uuid "dc8c6a94-f83d-5ddc-9ac7-16569e0af282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5824" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection/e8d572c16184c11917c8a0aeb2640002a4e83077b702f3b3da3f150a40704bec" :answer/id #uuid "60192c33-7a93-5f17-8dce-200e306cece4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8824" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection/b89e146a9009a826ad488f1b383cad20a34e838b9fe2abc1933108397e0c3b05" :answer/id #uuid "7dcd8160-d06a-5313-84d5-6ecdab82da90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8319" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2acb1cc-9f9c-5f20-8492-d276ff50db9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130239/selection/308676ee768935887597226eda63df3da76ab9c572f196f1924a76655ad73d6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-130239/selection/308676ee768935887597226eda63df3da76ab9c572f196f1924a76655ad73d6d" "q-130239/selection/f75878873391a8e8308fe21dad7c6dc11f9b4bac31093cc78c4db8e407a5de20" "q-130239/selection/d4cfd0801c2aff2cc8d8f0cdb705bc454b1338fe18b3a150e670f4b9fc2a70a3" "q-130239/selection/e8d572c16184c11917c8a0aeb2640002a4e83077b702f3b3da3f150a40704bec" "q-130239/selection/b89e146a9009a826ad488f1b383cad20a34e838b9fe2abc1933108397e0c3b05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130239" :question/id #uuid "219c0d97-8258-52bc-8ee4-ca2b0f52688a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130239" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ compute $P(X>5)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(0.7)^{x-1}(0.3), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>5.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4)+f(5) \\\\  & =(0.7)^{0}(0.3)+(0.7)^{1}(0.3)+(0.7)^{2}(0.3)+(0.7)^{3}(0.3)+(0.7)^{4}(0.3) \\\\  & ≈0.8319.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & ≈1-0.8319 \\\\  & =0.1681.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-130239/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection/98caeb1bf7b67c7e9ef28da889e95a562ba3d39a156a979319f325d651e79ea5" :answer/id #uuid "cf981415-71c6-569f-bc3e-b1cb8e1bf760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9744" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection/4f04d045988bd9de986c8cc00944460c9c48e4b168235ff9e0ed366f1cc9ac43" :answer/id #uuid "7d5de395-04ad-556b-92cd-5a142b6fc4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0102" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection/1c7377cfe77022295f565358a4585350e7209734e29c4a7a6a76a6ba0bb40afe" :answer/id #uuid "a53e5713-9608-51ea-bf5a-4e441e202486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3898" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection/95124fc05b9b3ff4889f1e88e0b827074007d935b712f9d00bb571068a1933f6" :answer/id #uuid "a1e747bd-b7c8-52e0-b776-543a4e42518f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9898" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection/3f5100d463c9047509ae95e7a26cb6dc03b2c9cda4c226509b3df4f0a549e313" :answer/id #uuid "11da7290-c20b-58fe-a027-bbde5905837d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0256" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7aab0506-70d9-5144-9f75-fa7dee3d0c8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130233/selection/3f5100d463c9047509ae95e7a26cb6dc03b2c9cda4c226509b3df4f0a549e313" :answer-field/choices ["q-130233/selection/98caeb1bf7b67c7e9ef28da889e95a562ba3d39a156a979319f325d651e79ea5" "q-130233/selection/4f04d045988bd9de986c8cc00944460c9c48e4b168235ff9e0ed366f1cc9ac43" "q-130233/selection/1c7377cfe77022295f565358a4585350e7209734e29c4a7a6a76a6ba0bb40afe" "q-130233/selection/95124fc05b9b3ff4889f1e88e0b827074007d935b712f9d00bb571068a1933f6" "q-130233/selection/3f5100d463c9047509ae95e7a26cb6dc03b2c9cda4c226509b3df4f0a549e313"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130233" :question/id #uuid "b1c4969e-7357-5e3f-b223-3e1743e3f17a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130233" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ compute $P(X\\ge 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{x-1}(\\frac{3}{5}), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 5.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =1-P(X<5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{5})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{5})+{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =0.9744.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =1-P(X<5) \\\\  & =1-0.9744 \\\\  & =0.0256.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection/7c22735505c32cb377f999917335240111eb879a64a30e182fb4de50be6eb650" :answer/id #uuid "1841346a-4636-586d-9b64-9994661d90e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.027" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection/a6568d47e052147e66c63837331997eef153bf8c3e8a0443293aee4bced4cab0" :answer/id #uuid "58749640-ef45-5d6a-a47d-7e8477253484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.932" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection/aa2e8587723de8de749134e746a21e7fc0676793f9da6c4f60c2cb7255fa7098" :answer/id #uuid "3915a24f-698e-5442-9422-3d61dea6ce0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.092" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection/4719b85a90b00181f834a30122d908b80772b1ebe444e6fe0d0577dcbb9a8dbe" :answer/id #uuid "d49af3ed-e963-5844-8f75-83a434537a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.973" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection/9f55e0bbfb13a4ab89d0a52b8b664141603b01561525eafac3b3d6b41ebc1b26" :answer/id #uuid "c494f012-1182-5589-8e43-bd03f8ad97b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.908" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a754b1a4-788e-5709-8a0e-9d1d9dba3b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97176/selection/7c22735505c32cb377f999917335240111eb879a64a30e182fb4de50be6eb650" :answer-field/choices ["q-97176/selection/7c22735505c32cb377f999917335240111eb879a64a30e182fb4de50be6eb650" "q-97176/selection/a6568d47e052147e66c63837331997eef153bf8c3e8a0443293aee4bced4cab0" "q-97176/selection/aa2e8587723de8de749134e746a21e7fc0676793f9da6c4f60c2cb7255fa7098" "q-97176/selection/4719b85a90b00181f834a30122d908b80772b1ebe444e6fe0d0577dcbb9a8dbe" "q-97176/selection/9f55e0bbfb13a4ab89d0a52b8b664141603b01561525eafac3b3d6b41ebc1b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97176" :question/id #uuid "0f41b6a4-50b1-5122-8260-283c4994a71d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97176" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ compute $P(X>3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.3)}^{x-1}(0.7), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.3)}^{0}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{1}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{2}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-0.973 \\\\  & =0.027.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-97176/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97176"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8553"] :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ compute $P(X = 3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/5973b712a92cadd7bc301f7e8e859a1a53a551cfeee0b0ac1404ddbfc352ac56.png)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/a7c5af2adc67390439a5d46933083b796c30fc55f0f1f5ff8cd9d374a905695d.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8554"] :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ compute $P(X < 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/e31c12bf515605c7cb46d96a55a8e2a3cab7eaeb5897bb04cfbe87d4d6cc6875.png)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/5e7f6f2abab85141723e1ef5bd97157968584623433cd5a3e4d0454a39ef000b.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.893\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto  $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8555"] :question/problem "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ compute $P(2 \\leq X \\leq 3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/e31c12bf515605c7cb46d96a55a8e2a3cab7eaeb5897bb04cfbe87d4d6cc6875.png)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/cb4d54529b778e27c44ea6611a366eef6e540d9de5343e3425797f03d51c54de.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in {2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{5})+{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8556"] :question/problem "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 56\\right),$ compute $P(X > 2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/ab3f034397a81b2369008754aef3c05f998f180b5127e543a05ab408c743cf8a.png)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 56\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069741/assets/efc7a45d9b19867340454ad32abe129214dcca021394f259f79d1e26643da5c7.png)\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X > 2.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{6})}^{0}(\\frac{5}{6})+{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{1}(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{35}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
